[al:新概念英语第一册]
[ti:Tea for Two]
[00:00.70]Lesson 125 | 第125课
[00:03.01]Tea for two | 两人喝茶
[00:05.89]Listen to the tape then answer this question. | 听录音，然后回答问题。
[00:10.78]Does Susan have tea by herself? | 苏珊独自一人喝茶吗？
[00:15.44]Can't you come in and have tea now, Peter? | 彼得，你现在不能进来喝茶吗？
[00:20.68]Not yet. | 还不能。
[00:22.24]I must water the garden first. | 我必须先浇花园。
[00:25.29]Do you have to water it now? | 你现在非浇不可吗？
[00:29.10]I'm afraid I must. | 恐怕非浇不可。
[00:31.53]Look at it! | 你瞧！
[00:32.84]It's terribly dry. | 干得厉害。
[00:35.16]What a nuisance! | 真讨厌！
[00:37.64]Last summer it was very dry, too. | 去年夏天也是很干。
[00:41.79]Don't you remember? | 你不记得了吗？
[00:44.00]I had to water it every day. | 我不得不每天浇水。
[00:47.22]Well, I'll have tea by myself. | 哎，我一个人喝茶了。
[00:51.88]That was quick! | 真快！
[00:54.34]Have you finished already? | 你已经浇完了吗？
[00:57.12]Yes. | 是的。
[00:58.51]Look out of the window. | 你往窗外看。
[01:00.91]It's raining! | 下雨了！
[01:03.05]That means you don't need to water the garden. | 这意味着你不用浇花园了。
[01:08.56]That was a pleasant surprise. | 这真是个意外的惊喜。
[01:11.96]It means I can have tea, instead. | 这意味着我可以去喝茶了。